// =============================================================================
//  iOS SIGNING — edit this to run the app on your own iPhone
// =============================================================================
//
//  Apple will not install an app on a physical device unless it is signed by a
//  developer account. A *free* Apple ID is enough for your own phone; the only
//  catch is that the app stops opening after seven days and you re-run this to
//  refresh it. A paid Apple Developer account ($99/yr) removes that.
//
//  Two things to do, once:
//
//  1. Add your Apple ID to Xcode.
//       Xcode → Settings → Accounts → + → Apple ID → sign in.
//
//  2. Put your Team ID below.
//       It is the 10-character code beside your name in that same Accounts
//       window, in the "Team" column — something like A1B2C3D4E5.
//       Or run:  open ios/Runner.xcworkspace  and read it from
//       Runner → Signing & Capabilities → Team.
//
//  Then: flutter run -d "Sengly’s Phone"
//
//  Two-word note on the phone itself: the first time you install, iOS refuses
//  to open an app from an unknown developer. Approve it once at
//  Settings → General → VPN & Device Management → your Apple ID → Trust.

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Your Apple Developer Team ID. Leave blank and the build will stop asking you
//  to pick a team in Xcode.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = DS92877RBP

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The app's unique identifier on the App Store and on the device.
//
//  Must be globally unique, so use a domain you control, reversed. If you do
//  not own a domain, your own name works fine for a personal build:
//      com.senglyvin.restaurantqr
//
//  Free Apple IDs sometimes reject an identifier that someone else has already
//  claimed — if the build complains, change this to something more unusual and
//  run again. Changing it makes iOS treat it as a different app, so the demo
//  data starts fresh.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_BUNDLE_ID = com.senglyvin.restaurantqr
